fact WorkItem(id: "WI-227", description: some(value: "Operation-call-model Phase E: emit requirement_at_sort and construct_requirement IR forms. WI-222 Phase D currently emits only requirement_at_current(slot=j) projections — sufficient for the v0 stdlib model where requires_chain is transitive-flat (every dep at top level). The other two IR forms from the design's call-rewrite cases (requirement_at_sort(chain, k) for nested-handle projections, construct_requirement(impl, [...]) for static dep construction) are unreachable in current paths because: (i) loader's collect_requires recurses transitively so caller chains never hold nested handles, (ii) Defer fires only when caller has the dep in chain so static construction isn't needed within Defer. They become reachable when WI-224 (full SLD) introduces conditional instances that recursively build requirement values and may emit nested chains. Scope: (a) refactor record_apply_within_rewrite's projection-building loop into a recursive search: try flat caller-slot lookup first, then nested via requires_chain of each caller slot's spec, then static construction via SortProvidesInfo lookup; (b) emit requirement_at_sort(requirement_at_current(i), k) when the dep lives bundled inside caller slot i; (c) emit construct_requirement(impl, sub_projections) when the dep is fully ground but not in caller chain; (d) tests for each emission path including synthetic scenarios that exercise the otherwise-unreachable branches. Acceptance: cargo-test green; new tests pin (1) flat path still emits requirement_at_current (regression); (2) synthetic nested-handle scenario emits requirement_at_sort chain; (3) ground-dep scenario emits construct_requirement. Reference: docs/design/operation-call-model.md §'Call rewrite cases', §'Two primitives: requirement_at_current and requirement_at_sort'."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-222"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-11T17:04:35Z"))
